// G4 PROGRAM THE VALIDATION IMAGE -- MCUboot + signed app, over SWD.
//
// THIS SCRIPT RESETS AND ERASES. It is the only one here that does, and it must
// never be pointed at a board carrying an uncollected corpse.
//
// SWD rather than OTA is not a preference. This image uses
// pm_static_v45_corpse.yml, which moves mcuboot_secondary's end address, and
// MCUboot compiles its own flash map in. Bootloader and application must be
// programmed together or they disagree about where the secondary slot ends and
// OTA silently stops working. merged.hex carries both.
//
// `erase` is a full chip erase of the code region. It does NOT touch UICR, so
// APPROTECT state is unchanged -- which is what we want, since the image does
// not lock it (CONFIG_NRF_APPROTECT_LOCK is not set) and locking it would end
// SWD access to this board permanently.
//
// Download verification is on (VerifyDownload = 1 in jlink_settings.ini), and
// the wrapper additionally reads the flash back in a SEPARATE J-Link session
// and compares it byte for byte. Same-session verification can be satisfied
// from a cache; a fresh session cannot.
si 1
speed 4000
device NRF52840_XXAA
connect
erase
loadfile MERGED_HEX_PATH
r
go
exit
